        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0f8456e4-f879-5b4e-af20-50cbe4c9f870",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Boyle, Danny Arnold, Michael Cavanaugh\n- TV Shows: Joe Bash, Barney Miller, The X-Files, The West Wing, Starman, Hunter, Monk, 24\n- Films: Joe\n- Organizations: New York City Police Department\n- Roles: TV producer, beat cop, guest-starring role\n\nFacts:\n- Danny Arnold created the television series \"Joe Bash\" after his successful New York City police detective sitcom \"Barney Miller\".\n- \"Joe Bash\" starred Peter Boyle as a weary and embittered New York City Police Department beat cop.\n- Peter Boyle's breakthrough performance was in the 1970 film \"Joe\".\n- Peter Boyle later won praise in both comedic and dramatic parts.\n- Peter Boyle won an Emmy Award in 1996 for a guest-starring role on the science-fiction drama \"The X-Files\".\n- Michael Cavanaugh's television guest credits include \"The West Wing,\" \"Joe Bash,\" \"Starman,\" \"Hunter,\" \"Monk,\" and \"24\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "0ca384f5-5339-5aa8-bc6d-93e5ff41281f",
        "text": "Page: Joe Bash. Sentence: Starring Peter Boyle as a weary and embittered New York City Police Department beat cop, it was created by veteran TV producer Danny Arnold following his successful New York City police detective sitcom \"Barney Miller\".\nPage: Peter Boyle. Sentence: Boyle, who won an Emmy Award in 1996 for a guest-starring role on the science-fiction drama \"The X-Files\", won praise in both comedic and dramatic parts following his breakthrough performance in the 1970 film \"Joe\".\nPage: Michael Cavanaugh (actor). Sentence: His television guest-credits include \"The West Wing\", \"Joe Bash\", \"Starman\", \"Hunter\", \"Monk\" and \"24\".",
